(174,1,'2026-04-08 06:04:28','2026-04-08 06:04:28','The IEEE EMBS Student Chapter actively participated in Clubs/Chapters Day at Khalifa University, an annual event designed to introduce students to the diverse technical and professional clubs/chapters available on campus.\n\nThis initiative served as a platform to showcase the importance of biomedical engineering, promote collaboration, and encourage student involvement in research and innovation.\n\n<strong>Key Objectives:</strong>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Increase awareness of the EMBS Chapter and its role in improving biomedical engineering advancements.</li>\n 	<li>Engage students in discussions about emerging technologies in healthcare, AI-driven medical solutions, and biomechanics.</li>\n 	<li>Recruit new members by highlighting the benefits of participating in IEEE EMBS activities, including workshops, research opportunities, and industry connections.</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Activities during the event:</strong>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Stroop Color Word Task that measures mental stress.</li>\n 	<li>Detecting and printing the ECG signal (Pulse Rate).</li>\n 	<li>Arranging the brain layers in the correct order.</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Impact and Outcomes:</strong>\n<ul>\n 	<li><strong>Enhanced Membership Growth:</strong> The event successfully attracted new student members, expanding the chapter’s reach within the university.</li>\n 	<li><strong>Increased Engagement:</strong> Numerous students expressed interest in upcoming technical workshops, mentorship programs, and research collaborations facilitated by the chapter.</li>\n</ul>','Clubs & Chapters Day','','inherit','closed','closed','','153-autosave-v1','','','2026-04-08 06:04:28','2026-04-08 06:04:28','',153,'http://127.0.0.1:8001/?p=174',0,'revision','',0),
