(208,1,'2026-04-08 07:13:31','2026-04-08 07:13:31','The <strong>IEEE EMBS KU Chapter</strong> played a pivotal role in organizing and hosting the <strong>11th International Conference on Software Development and Technologies for Enhancing Accessibility and Fighting Info-Exclusion (DSAI 2024)</strong>. This event, scheduled for <strong>November 13-15, 2024</strong>, focused on software and web accessibility, human-computer interaction, e-health, and inclusive technologies.\n\n<strong>Key Contributions:</strong>\n<ul>\n 	<li><strong>Conference Organization:</strong>The chapter actively collaborated in <strong>planning, logistics, and execution</strong>, ensuring a seamless experience for attendees, speakers, and researchers.</li>\n 	<li><strong>Technical Engagement:</strong>Members participated in <strong>peer-review processes, special track coordination, and technical support</strong>, fostering a high-quality academic environment.</li>\n 	<li>The event provided a <strong>platform for students and faculty</strong>to engage with cutting-edge research, encouraging interdisciplinary discussions in <strong>AI, accessibility, and e-health</strong>.</li>\n 	<li><strong>Global Networking:</strong>By co-hosting this international conference, the chapter <strong>enhanced its global visibility</strong>, attracting renowned researchers and industry professionals.</li>\n</ul>\nThis event provided the <strong>IEEE EMBS Student Chapter at Khalifa University</strong> with the opportunity to join the <strong>organizing committees</strong> for the <strong>7th International Conference on Activity and Behavior Computing (ABC 2025)</strong> and the <strong>21st IEEE Biomedical Circuits and Systems Conference (BioCas 2025)</strong>, further strengthening the chapter’s role in the global biomedical engineering community.\n\n&nbsp;','DSAI 2024 Conference','','inherit','closed','closed','','149-autosave-v1','','','2026-04-08 07:13:31','2026-04-08 07:13:31','',149,'http://127.0.0.1:8001/?p=208',0,'revision','',0),
(209,1,'2026-04-08 07:47:08','2026-04-08 07:47:08','','25','','inherit','open','closed','','25','','','2026-04-08 07:47:08','2026-04-08 07:47:08','',146,'http://127.0.0.1:8001/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/25.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(210,1,'2026-04-08 07:47:22','2026-04-08 07:47:22','Khalifa University was honored to host Professor Jonathan Knowles from University College London for a research seminar on “Future Biomaterials: Biomedical, Medicine, and Other Applications” on Wednesday, February 19, 2025, at the Main Campus Auditorium. As UCL’s most highly cited materials scientist and a global leader in biomaterials research, Professor Knowles shared insights from his extensive career, which spans over 400 publications and numerous international collaborations.\nDuring the seminar, Professor Knowles discussed the evolution of degradable biomaterials, from hydroxyapatite for bone grafting to cutting-edge 3D-printed resins for maxillofacial applications. He also highlighted recent advancements in nerve regeneration using innovative conduits developed with Dankook University. The event offered a valuable opportunity for attendees to explore the intersection of materials science, medicine, and clinical innovation.','The Future of Biomaterials','','inherit','closed','closed','','146-autosave-v1','','','2026-04-08 07:47:22','2026-04-08 07:47:22','',146,'http://127.0.0.1:8001/?p=210',0,'revision','',0),
