(214,1,'2026-04-08 07:50:38','2026-04-08 07:50:38','This seminar on bioelectronic devices for neural interfacing by Professor Christopher Proctor. His insights into flexible electronics, conducting polymers, and microfluidic integration showcased how these innovations are actually transforming diagnostics and therapy. The seminar focused on the emerging field of bioelectronic devices for neural interfacing, exploring how advanced technologies are bridging the gap between electronics and biological systems. These technologies are paving the way for more effective neural interfaces, with potential applications in medical diagnostics, therapy, and personalized healthcare. \n\nThe seminar was organized by the EMBS students\' chapter at Khalifa University in collaboration with the Collage of Medicine and Health Sciences (CMHS) and the Biomedical Engineering Department (BME).','Extending the Reach of Bioelectronic Implants','','inherit','closed','closed','','143-autosave-v1','','','2026-04-08 07:50:38','2026-04-08 07:50:38','',143,'http://127.0.0.1:8001/?p=214',0,'revision','',0),
